<p><strong>A walk-in queue works when arrivals are written down in order, clients are told an honest wait, and the next free chair goes to the next person without bumping a booked appointment.</strong></p>
<p><em>The scene below is a typical one, not a single named customer.</em></p>
<h2>Friday evening at the door</h2>
<p>Six people are standing in the shop. Nobody knows who came first. One says "I was here before him". The barber has a booked client arriving in ten minutes, and the walk-in who just sat down is not going to be finished by then.</p>
<h2>Walk-in queue or waiting list?</h2>
<p>They are different, and customers search for both.</p>
<ul><li><strong>A walk-in queue</strong> is for people in the shop now, waiting for the next chair.</li><li><strong>A waiting list</strong> is for people who want a slot that is full and will be offered it if it opens. See <a href="/blog/waiting-list-management-spa-salon-nepal/">waiting list management</a>.</li></ul>
<h2>How to run a walk-in queue</h2>
<ol><li><strong>Write every arrival down in order</strong> with the service they want.</li><li><strong>Estimate the wait from the schedule,</strong> not from memory: the next free gap and the real length of the service.</li><li><strong>Protect booked clients.</strong> A walk-in goes where there is actually time.</li><li><strong>Tell people their turn</strong> so they can wait outside or come back.</li></ol>
<h2>How Zennly helps</h2>
<p>Zennly has a <strong>live walk-in queue</strong> that shows each person's place in line and an estimated wait, so staff can give a real time instead of a guess. Walk-ins are fitted into the open gaps on each staff member's schedule, so they never collide with booked work, and every booking holds the staff member and the real length of the service. Zennly also has a waiting list for people who want a full slot. See <a href="/solutions/barbershop/">software for barbershops</a>.</p>
<h2>A quick fix you can start today</h2>
<ol><li>Keep one list at the door, in order of arrival.</li><li>Check the schedule before promising a time.</li><li>Offer online booking to regulars so the queue stays short.</li></ol>
